+# Verification: multi-turn Q&A conversation history
+
+Date: 2026-11-15 · Electron 33 on macOS · results from the latest run.
+
+## How to reproduce
+
+```bash
+npm install
+npm run check
+bash scripts/check-architecture.sh
+npm test
+npm run build && node --experimental-websocket scripts/verify-conversation.mjs
+```
+
+If your shell exports `NODE_OPTIONS=--openssl-legacy-provider`, Electron refuses
+to start (`npm run dev` included). The verify script clears it for the child
+process; for manual runs use `NODE_OPTIONS= npm run dev`.
+
+## End-to-end results (`scripts/verify-conversation.mjs`, real Electron app)
+
+```
+PASS  empty state shown when there is no history
+PASS  pending indicator while asking #1
+PASS  pending indicator while asking #2
+PASS  pending indicator while asking #3
+PASS  all questions shown in order — ["How is the architecture designed?","What does the meeting summary say?","qwxz flurb?"]
+PASS  answers shown in full (match persisted text)
+PASS  each exchange shows question + answer timestamps — ["Today, 10:21 PM","2026-11-16T01:21:59.601Z"]
+PASS  answer citations show document and excerpt — "[1]\ndesign-notes · chunk 0\n# Software Design Notes\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nTh"
+PASS  answer without citations is labelled
+PASS  clicking a citation opens the cited document
+PASS  follow-up context chip appears and input is focused
+PASS  follow-up is linked to its parent and answered in context — sources=2
+PASS  copy answer gives feedback — Copied
+PASS  IPC error shown with retry
+PASS  retry succeeds and error clears
+PASS  long answer collapses and expands to full text — 1200 -> 3190
+PASS  legacy entry gets a readable older-date timestamp — Mar 4, 2025, 07:00 AM
+PASS  page does not scroll horizontally
+PASS  selecting a past question focuses that exchange
+PASS  selected exchange is scrolled into view
+PASS  conversation persists across app restart
+PASS  clear conversation returns to empty state
+PASS  structured ASK_QUESTION / GET_CONVERSATION logs emitted
+23/23 checks passed
+```
+
+Sample documents are seeded through the preload API because the starter's
+"+ Import" button is a no-op (see known issues).
+
+## Screenshots
+
+| File | Shows |
+|---|---|
+| `01-empty.png` | Empty history state |
+| `02-conversation.png` | Several exchanges: question/answer bubbles, timestamps, confidence, sources, answer with no sources |
+| `03-citation-opens-document.png` | Clicking a citation opens the cited document above the conversation |
+| `04-error.png` | Failed question shown in the thread with Retry / Dismiss |
+| `05-long-answer.png` | Long answer collapsed with "Show full answer"; older timestamp with the year |
+| `06-history-select.png` | Sidebar History index; the selected exchange is scrolled into view and focused |
+
+## Known issues outside this feature (not fixed)
+
+1. "+ Import" button only logs to the console. There is no way to import from the UI.
+2. "Index Document" (single document) writes chunks but not `index-meta.json`, so those chunks are never used by Q&A. Only batch `indexing.start()` feeds Q&A.
+3. The status bar shows empty `Index:` / `Documents:` values because `indexing.status()` returns `IndexStatus` and not `AppStatus`.
+4. Mock answers include a raw 100-character slice of the excerpt (e.g. "follows a layered ."). This comes from the starter's answer generator.
